## Implementation Design — Team Scope sync logic

### Context finding (critical)

`syncDocument(docId)` runs in two distinct contexts:
- **Context ①** (Workspace Add-on sidebar — active user): triggered by "Sync now" button.
- **Context ④** (timed sweep `syncAll`, `onActionSheetEdit` — sheet owner): no active Doc binding.

`PropertiesService.getDocumentProperties()` is only valid in context ①; in context ④ it returns the
ActionSheet's properties. Therefore `teamScope` MUST be stored as a **Drive file `appProperty`**
(via Drive REST API), which is accessible from any context via `UrlFetchApp`. Property key: `teamScope`.

Drive `appProperties` are scoped per OAuth client (private, not user-scoped), so they are
consistent regardless of which user or trigger runs the sync.

---

### Schema references (ContractSchema.js)

- TeamData columns: `team_id=1`, `folder_id=2`, `contact=3`. Tab name: `'TeamData'`.
- DocData columns: `file_id=1`, `doc_name=2`, `doc_modified=3`, `doc_updated=4`,
  `sync_status=5`, `team_id=6`, `action_count=7`, `resolved_count=8`. Tab name: `'DocData'`.
- Actions `file_id` is column 2 (already in schema). Current sync payload does not send it →
  EPIC-B adds `fileId` to `_syncActionRows` payload so WebApp can write it.

---

### New helper functions (all in SyncManager.js)

#### `_getDocAppProperty(docId, key, token)`
Reads a Drive file `appProperty` via Drive REST API.
```
GET https://www.googleapis.com/drive/v3/files/{docId}?fields=appProperties
Authorization: Bearer {token}
Returns: appProperties object or null on failure
```
Returns the value for `key`, or `null` if absent or on API error.

#### `_setDocAppProperty(docId, key, value, token)`
Writes a Drive file `appProperty` via Drive REST API.
```
PATCH https://www.googleapis.com/drive/v3/files/{docId}?fields=appProperties
Authorization: Bearer {token}
Body: { appProperties: { [key]: value } }
```
No-op / logs warning on failure. Does not throw.

#### `_readTeamDataRows(ss)`
Reads all TeamData rows from the `TeamData` tab.
```js
var sheet = ss.getSheetByName('TeamData');
// Returns: [{ teamId, folderId, contact }, ...] (skip blank rows)
// Uses CONTRACT_SCHEMA.sheetTeamData.columnsByField
```
Returns `[]` if the tab is missing or has no data rows.

#### `_walkFolderForTeam(docId, teamDataRows)`
Walks the Drive folder ancestry of `docId`, checking each folder ID against `teamDataRows`.
```js
// 1. DriveApp.getFileById(docId).getParents()  → first parent folder iterator
// 2. While folder exists and is not root:
//    a. Check folder.getId() against teamDataRows[i].folderId (exact match)
//    b. First match: return { teamId: row.teamId }
//    c. Move to folder.getParents() → next ancestor
// 3. No match: return null
// Log 'sync.teamScope.walk.no-match' { docId } when returning null
// Log 'sync.teamScope.walk.multi-parent' { docId } when a folder has >1 parent (use first)
```
Returns `{ teamId }` on match, `null` on no match.
Drive errors (permission denied, quota) → log `sync.teamScope.walk.error`, return `null`.

#### `_getOrUpsertDocDataRow(ss, fileId, docName, docModified, teamId, syncStatus, actionCount, resolvedCount)`
Reads the DocData tab for the row matching `fileId` (col 1). If found, updates in place;
if not found, appends a new row. Returns the current row data (post-write).
```js
// Find: scan col 1 for exact match on fileId
// Write all 8 columns atomically via setValues()
// doc_updated = new Date() (always set to now)
```

#### `_readDocDataRow(ss, docId)`
Reads the single DocData row whose `file_id` (col 1) matches `docId`. Read-only — no write.
```js
// 1. var sheet = ss.getSheetByName('DocData'); if missing → return null
// 2. Scan col 1 (file_id) for exact match on docId
// 3. On match, return:
//    { fileId, docName, docModified, docUpdated, syncStatus, teamId, actionCount, resolvedCount }
//    mapped via CONTRACT_SCHEMA.sheetDocData.columnsByField
// 4. No match → return null
```
Used by `_syncTeamScope` to read the current `syncStatus`/`teamId` before the upsert decision.

#### `assertTeamAccess(teamId, ss)`
Verifies the active user can access the team's folder.
```js
// 1. _readTeamDataRows(ss) → find first row where teamId matches
// 2. If no row found: throw new Error('TeamNotFound: ' + teamId)
// 3. DriveApp.getFolderById(row.folderId)  → throws on access denial
// 4. On catch: throw new Error('TeamAccessDenied: ' + teamId)
```
Callers catch `TeamAccessDenied` / `TeamNotFound` and return no rows + an error surface.
(This function is not called inside `syncDocument`; it is used by Import/Notify, EPIC-D/E.)

---

### Insertion point in `syncDocument()`

Insert the team-scope block immediately after the trash check and before `_assignPlaceholderTokens`.
The block requires `docId`, `doc` (the open DocumentApp doc object), and `token`.

```
[existing: open doc + trash check]
↓
[NEW] _syncTeamScope(ss, docId, token)
↓
[existing: _assignPlaceholderTokens]
[existing: _scanFloatingActions]
[existing: _syncActionRows  ← add fileId to payload]
...
```

#### `_syncTeamScope(ss, docId, token)` (orchestrator — private)
```js
function _syncTeamScope(ss, docId, token) {
  var teamDataRows = _readTeamDataRows(ss);
  var docDataRow   = _readDocDataRow(ss, docId);   // read-only; upsert happens later
  var teamScope    = _getDocAppProperty(docId, 'teamScope', token);

  // UpdateDoc override: DocData wins
  if (docDataRow && docDataRow.syncStatus === 'UpdateDoc') {
    teamScope = docDataRow.teamId;
    _setDocAppProperty(docId, 'teamScope', teamScope, token);
    GasLogger.log('sync.teamScope.overridden', { docId: docId, teamId: teamScope });
    // Clear SyncStatus via _upsertDocDataRow (syncStatus = '')
  }
  // Auto-assign: walk folders on first encounter
  else if (!teamScope) {
    var found = _walkFolderForTeam(docId, teamDataRows);
    if (found) {
      teamScope = found.teamId;
      _setDocAppProperty(docId, 'teamScope', teamScope, token);
      GasLogger.log('sync.teamScope.resolved', { docId: docId, teamId: teamScope });
    }
    // else: stays blank; logged inside _walkFolderForTeam
  }
  // else: teamScope already set → STICKY (deliberate). Moving the doc to a different folder
  //   does NOT re-walk or reassign — DocWins, just mirror to DocData below. The only path that
  //   changes an already-set teamScope is the UpdateDoc override branch above.

  // Upsert DocData with current teamScope
  // action/resolved counts computed after scan (pass 0 here; WebApp will correct via sync_action_rows)
  // syncStatus cleared if it was UpdateDoc, otherwise unchanged
  var newSyncStatus = (docDataRow && docDataRow.syncStatus === 'UpdateDoc') ? '' : (docDataRow ? docDataRow.syncStatus : '');
  _getOrUpsertDocDataRow(ss, docId, /* docName */ '', new Date(), teamScope || '', newSyncStatus, 0, 0);
}
```

`docName` and the counts are updated by the WebApp's `sync_action_rows` handler (which already
receives `docTitle`). The team scope upsert here is a first-pass write; WebApp will update counts
on its write. This avoids a second full-table read after the scan.

---

### `_syncActionRows` payload change

Add `fileId: docId` to the POST payload so the WebApp can write `File Id` (col 2) on upsert.
This change lands in the `[IMP] Add Team Scope property read/write` bead.

---

### Log tags (completion signals)

| Tag | Condition |
|-----|-----------|
| `sync.teamScope.resolved` | Auto-assignment found a match |
| `sync.teamScope.overridden` | UpdateDoc path applied |
| `sync.teamScope.walk.no-match` | No ancestor folder matched |
| `sync.teamScope.walk.error` | Drive API error during walk |
| `sync.teamScope.walk.multi-parent` | Folder had >1 parent; used first |

---

### Edge cases

- **Drive quota during folder walk**: `_walkFolderForTeam` catches and logs; `teamScope` stays blank.
- **TeamData tab missing**: `_readTeamDataRows` returns `[]`; walk finds no match; logs no-match.
- **`UpdateDoc` with blank/invalid Team Id**: `_syncTeamScope` sets teamScope to the blank string;
  log a warning `sync.teamScope.override-blank`; clear SyncStatus anyway to avoid a stuck loop.
- **Multiple parent folders**: use `iter.next()` (first result); log `multi-parent` warning.
- **Sticky assignment (doc moved)**: once `teamScope` is set, relocating the doc to a different
  folder does NOT trigger a re-walk or reassignment — even if the new folder matches a different
  TeamData row. Reassignment occurs only through the `SyncStatus == 'UpdateDoc'` override. This is
  the intended boundary shared by me6w.3 (auto-assign) and me6w.4 (override).
- **Idempotency**: if `teamScope` is already set and `SyncStatus` is not `UpdateDoc`, the block
  reads teamScope once and writes DocData (no Drive walk, no property write) — effectively a no-op
  for Drive API calls.

---

### Bead assignment guide

Each `[IMP]` bead gets one piece of this design as its sole work scope:

| Bead me6w.3 | Add Team Scope property read/write + folder-walk auto-assignment |
|------------|------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Scope | `_getDocAppProperty`, `_setDocAppProperty`, `_readTeamDataRows`, `_walkFolderForTeam`, `_syncTeamScope` (orchestrator) + `fileId` in sync payload |
| Entry point | `syncDocument` (extended) |
| Log tag | `sync.teamScope.resolved`, `sync.teamScope.walk.*` |

| Bead me6w.4 | Sync Team Scope with DocData (DocWins + UpdateDoc write-back) |
|------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|
| Scope | `_readDocDataRow`, `_getOrUpsertDocDataRow`, UpdateDoc path inside `_syncTeamScope` |
| Entry point | `syncDocument` (extended) |
| Log tag | `sync.teamScope.overridden` |

| Bead me6w.5 | Enforce team-scoped security gate |
|------------|----------------------------------|
| Scope | `assertTeamAccess(teamId, ss)` function — standalone, not called in `syncDocument` |
| Entry point | Called by future Import/Notify; add to `TestWebApp.js` test routes for test-harness coverage |
| Log tag | none (throws on failure) |
